["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Be on the glass when the bear is on the food. This chapter is the clock, and how weather and people bend it.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Mainly daytime, with dawn and dusk peaks (65 to 75%).</li><li>Near people, more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Feed, bed and water through a day; dawn and dusk; heat, rain, wind, cold and snow, the moon, and hunting pressure; each with how sure we are.</li><li>Evidence levels: a % means a source; Tip means hunter experience; <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> means no good data found.</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-05\">Chapter 5, The year</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-black-bear-07\">Chapter 7, Where they are</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cross section of black bear country from creek to ridge. Creek bottom: fish where they run, shrubs and berries. Grassy south facing slope: first green food in spring. Cutblock: berries in summer and fall. Timber: beds and cover next to the food. Avalanche chute higher up: spring and summer greens. From the BC account: spring meadows, riparian, skunk cabbage, avalanche chutes, grassy south slopes, burns.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bear country in one slice</text><path d=\"M0 260 L60 250 L120 200 L190 150 L250 110 L310 70 L360 50 L400 45 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M0 262 Q40 258 80 262 L80 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"/><g transform=\"translate(250 110) scale(0.6)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(270 100) scale(0.7)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(290 88) scale(0.6)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(230 128) scale(0.5)\"><polygon points=\"0,-60 -18,0 18,0\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"-3\" y=\"0\" width=\"6\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(150 180) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(185 158) scale(0.8)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><path d=\"M335 55 L345 52 L360 130 L345 130 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Creek</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Grassy south slope</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cutblock berries</text><text x=\"318\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Timber: beds</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Avalanche chute</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Spring low, summer up, fall berries, fish</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Feeds, then beds in cover close by (Tip).</li><li>Travels in cover between food sites <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the daily loop in detail</summary><ul><li>Home ranges are \"several feeding areas connected by travel routes... often located in wooded areas that provide cover\" (90%, BC account).</li><li>Day beds: shallow scrapes in thick cover or at the base of a big tree near food (Tip, chapter 8).</li><li>Hot days: water and shade in creek bottoms (Tip, quick lesson).</li><li>In hyperphagia a bear may forage up to about 20 hours a day (65%, agency and news reports); feeding stretches into midday in cool fall weather (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>WildSafeBC: \"mainly diurnal\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Glass the first and last 2 hours hardest (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: timing with evidence</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mainly active by day</td><td>75%, WildSafeBC</td></tr><tr><td>Dawn and dusk peaks</td><td>70%, quick lesson and BearWise</td></tr><tr><td>Shifts to night near people</td><td>75%, WildSafeBC; 65%, Massachusetts GPS (Global Positioning System) study of 86 bears</td></tr><tr><td>Feeds most of the day in fall</td><td>65%, hyperphagia reports</td></tr><tr><td>Big boars use the last light</td><td>Tip</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Legal hours for bear: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, page 11, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>). No lights, no infrared optics <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"regs\" data-regs=\"r3bear\"></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Weather and black bears, with how sure we are. Hot afternoon: beds in shade near water, tip. Cool cloudy day: feeds longer in daylight, tip. Rain: keeps feeding and you move quieter, tip. Hard wind: its nose and ears are less sure, tip. First real cold and snow: nudges bears toward the den, 70 percent. Moon: no good bear data found, VERIFY.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Weather and bears: how sure?</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hot afternoon</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shade, near water</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"56\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"90\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Cool, cloudy</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Feeds longer</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"96\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"130\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rain</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Keeps feeding</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"136\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"170\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Hard wind</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Senses less sure</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"176\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"210\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">First cold, snow</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Nudges to den</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"216\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">70%</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">Moon</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"start\">No bear data</text><rect x=\"326\" y=\"256\" width=\"58\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">VERIFY</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Most weather effects are hunter experience, not studies (Tip).</li></ul><ul><li>No good bear data on the moon: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather in detail</summary><ul><li>Heat: bears bed in shade and near water on hot afternoons (Tip). Early fall heat pushes feeding to dawn and dusk (Tip).</li><li>Cool, cloudy days: longer daylight feeding (Tip).</li><li>Rain: feeding continues; wet ground lets you move quietly (Tip).</li><li>Wind: hard gusts swirl scent and noise; hunt sheltered slopes (Tip, <a href=\"#/s/wind-mastery\">wind mastery</a>).</li><li>Cold weather makes bears \"increasingly lethargic\" before denning (90%, BC account). A first heavy snow as the den trigger is common hunter belief (Tip).</li><li>Barometric pressure and the moon: no bear studies found (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>). For deer, no moon effect was found (70%, <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-06\">mule deer chapter 6</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of one day on a slope. The sun rises and crosses the sky. In the morning the sun warms the slope and blue arrows show air rising uphill. Near sunset the air swirls as the thermals switch. In the evening the slope cools and the arrows flow downhill. Morning: be above the deer. Evening: be below.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fdf1d6\"><animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#fdf1d6;#fffaf0;#e9dfcf\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><g><circle r=\"16\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><animateMotion dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\" keyPoints=\"0;0.8;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.4;1\" calcMode=\"linear\" path=\"M40 150 Q 200 -40 380 150\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0.5\" keyTimes=\"0;0.7;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path d=\"M0 270 L300 90 L400 90 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"320,90 330,60 340,90\"/><polygon points=\"350,90 360,56 370,90\"/></g><g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M27.7 225.4 L68.8 200.7 M61.6 212.0 L68.8 200.7 L55.4 201.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M117.7 171.4 L158.8 146.7 M151.6 158.0 L158.8 146.7 L145.4 147.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M207.7 117.4 L248.8 92.7 M241.6 104.0 L248.8 92.7 L235.4 93.8\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;22.3 -13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Morning: sun warms the slope</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air rises UPHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.31;0.33;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M90 200 c 20 -30, 50 -10, 30 10 c -15 15, -30 -5, -15 -15\"/><path d=\"M200 140 c -20 -30, -50 -10, -30 10 c 15 15, 30 -5, 15 -15\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Near sunset: the switch</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air swirls, mixed</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><g><path d=\"M68.8 200.7 L27.7 225.4 M41.0 224.4 L27.7 225.4 L34.9 214.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M158.8 146.7 L117.7 171.4 M131.0 170.4 L117.7 171.4 L124.9 160.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M248.8 92.7 L207.7 117.4 M221.0 116.4 L207.7 117.4 L214.9 106.1\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-22.3 13.4\" dur=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"12\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">Evening: slope cools</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Air sinks DOWNHILL</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.65;0.67;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"190\" y=\"230\" width=\"200\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"254\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: be above</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Evening: be below</text></g></svg>\n<figcaption>The day's air: up in the morning, down at night. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: a black bear feeds in a berry patch above you. At first the wind blows from the bear toward you, so your scent cone trails behind you, away from the bear. Then the wind swings around and your scent cone swings toward the bear. The bear lifts its head: it smells you. Check the wind before every move.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent rides the wind</text><g transform=\"translate(120 92) scale(1.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(250 84) scale(1.1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(320 110) scale(1)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"26\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-2\" cy=\"-9\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-2\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"4\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"4\" cy=\"5\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(200 100)\"><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) scale(0.7 0.7)\"><rect x=\"-38\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"24\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><rect x=\"34\" y=\"8\" width=\"11\" height=\"28\" rx=\"5.5\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M-46 6 Q-52 -28 -24 -30 Q0 -26 26 -22 Q46 -18 46 4 Q30 24 -30 22 Q-46 20 -46 6 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M40 -20 L62 -16 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L56 4 Q44 2 40 -20 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M48 -18 L50 -32 L56 -18 Z\" fill=\"#1d1d1b\"/><path d=\"M66 -10 L78 -8 Q82 -2 76 0 L64 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b6a4a\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#eee\"/></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;-10\" keyTimes=\"0;0.9;1\" begin=\"0s\" dur=\"6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g transform=\"translate(200 250)\"><g><path d=\"M0 0 L-50 70 L50 70 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".22\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;0;180\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"6\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">You</text></g><g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><g><path d=\"M40 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10 M360 60 v40 m-6 -10 l6 10 l6 -10\" fill=\"none\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 200 150;0 200 150;180 200 150\" keyTimes=\"0;0.55;0.8\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g><g><text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind: bear to you. Good.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.6\" dur=\"7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"140\" width=\"250\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">Wind swung. Bear smells you.</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>One whiff and a pressured bear goes nocturnal. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Bears near people feed more at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Bumped bears come back after dark, if at all (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in detail</summary><ul><li>WildSafeBC: bears are mainly diurnal \"but may feed at night in high risk, human active areas\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Massachusetts GPS (Global Positioning System) collars on 86 bears: in developed areas bears moved their foraging to night (65%, secondary write up).</li><li>A road hunted cutblock sees the most pressure. Walk past the gate or glass across the valley (Tip).</li><li>Do not walk through the same patch every evening; glass it from far away (Tip).</li><li>Spring bear hunters crowd the first green road edges; the far side of the valley gets less traffic (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Plan (Tip)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1 hour before sunrise</td><td>On a glassing knob before light</td></tr><tr><td>Sunrise to 9:00</td><td>Glass berry slopes and cutblock edges</td></tr><tr><td>9:00 to 15:00</td><td>Scout sign, hang trail cameras, check the wind</td></tr><tr><td>15:00 to sunset</td><td>Back on glass over the best food</td></tr><tr><td>Last light</td><td>Stay until 1 hour after sunset, then out safely</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Legal hours are the frame; the bear decides inside it (Tip).</li><li>Plan with the <a href=\"#/plan\">planner</a> and the <a href=\"#/s/local-heffley\">Heffley Creek</a> page.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"24 hour clock of a typical fall black bear day. Feeding peaks at dawn and dusk, shown in orange, about 6 to 8:30 in the morning and 4:30 to 7:30 in the evening. Through the day it feeds and beds in shade, shown in sage. Night is mostly rest, but near people bears feed more at night. Times are typical, not exact.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A fall bear day (typical)</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"100\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><path d=\"M107.6 117.7 A100 100 0 0 1 300.0 156.0 L270.0 156.0 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 129.2 Z\" fill=\"#3d4a5c\"/><path d=\"M300.0 156.0 A100 100 0 0 1 279.3 216.9 L255.5 198.6 A70 70 0 0 0 270.0 156.0 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M279.3 216.9 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 194.3 L135.3 182.8 A70 70 0 0 0 255.5 198.6 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M107.6 194.3 A100 100 0 0 1 107.6 117.7 L135.3 129.2 A70 70 0 0 0 135.3 182.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"47.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"314.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"280.61017305526644\" y=\"241.61017305526642\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"275.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"119.38982694473358\" y=\"241.61017305526644\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"161.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text><text x=\"119.38982694473357\" y=\"80.38982694473358\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"156\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Orange: feeding</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">peaks dawn, dusk</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sage: feeds</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">and beds in shade</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Near people: more feeding at night (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"First light, last light, bears are in sight.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 1 and 1: hunt 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion, Jim Shockey via Boone and Crockett): \"The big bear holds the best food at the best time.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 20: up to about 20 hours a day of fall foraging <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Hot noon, shady bed; cool day, longer spread.\"</li><li><strong>Tip:</strong> glass the far side, not the road side.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Leaving the glass at 9:00 in October, when bears feed longer in cool weather.</li><li>Driving the same road every evening.</li><li>Believing moon rules for bears with no data.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Pick one cutblock. Glass it at dawn, noon and dusk on one day and log every bear in the Journal.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>WildSafeBC, <a href=\"https://wildsafebc.com/species/black-bear/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Black bear</a>, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>BC Ministry of Environment, Lands and Parks (2001), <a href=\"https://www.env.gov.bc.ca/wld/documents/blackbear.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Black Bears in British Columbia\"</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span></li><li>Geography Realm, <a href=\"https://www.geographyrealm.com/gps-tracking-shows-that-black-bears-avoid-humans-during-the-day/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPS (Global Positioning System) tracking shows black bears avoid humans during the day</a> (Massachusetts study of 86 bears), search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>Hyperphagia foraging hours: town and agency pages (Lake Lure, North Carolina Wildlife Resources Commission via WLOS television news), search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li><li>BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a>: page 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-black-bear.md</code>.</li></ul>"]